 "_note": "v7 = v6 with the preference legs REBUILT as SHORT COMPLETE TURNS and with the train/eval format mismatch fixed in evals.py. (1) Preference legs now FILTER for pairs whose responses are naturally <=96 tokens and prompts <=256 \u2014 no mid-sentence truncation, no tail-capped prompts. Discard is brutal by design (HelpSteer2 keeps 127 of 10162 pairs; its responses are inherently long) \u2014 a truncated turn ends mid-sentence and is not something the model ever saw. (2) evals.py now tokenises eval prompts as f'{prompt}\\n', matching data.py format_row, so the model is scored on the prefix shape it was TRAINED on. That changes EVERY leg's absolute numbers, so v7 results are NOT comparable to v6/earlier \u2014 this is a fresh baseline by design. (3) evaluate_mcq now reports discarded_examples and warns above 2%; the prompt cap is derived from max_length instead of guessed. hs2_cor_val dropped (62 rows, 6.4pt floor)."
}